  summary: "From 1906 to 1935 Ethiopia was dominated by a power struggle among the ruling elites. Menilek's stroke and the death of Ras Mekonnen opened the succession question, and the colonial powers signed the Tripartite Treaty of 1906. Menilek created the first cabinet in 1907 and named Lij Iyasu as successor in 1909. Iyasu ruled from 1911 to 1916 and was deposed, after which Zewditu and Ras Teferi shared power in the diarchy. Teferi removed his rivals, won at Anchim in 1930 and was crowned Emperor Haile Selassie, whose 1931 constitution gave his autocratic rule a legal basis.",
